cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Semantic Entropy Hallucination Detection"
message: "If you use this project, please cite it. Also cite Farquhar et al. (2024) for semantic entropy."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
abstract: >-
  Exploratory research code comparing semantic entropy, token predictive entropy and hidden-state
  features for question-level correctness prediction (100-question TriviaQA sample, Qwen3-1.7B).
  An experimental adaptation of semantic entropy, not a validated hallucination detector.
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Tirth Sanjaykumar
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tirth-2006/Sementicbyobi"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - semantic entropy
  - uncertainty estimation
  - hallucination
  - large language models
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Detecting hallucinations in large language models using semantic entropy"
    authors:
      - family-names: Farquhar
        given-names: Sebastian
    journal: Nature
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07421-0
